# Copy to .env.local and fill in. .env.local is gitignored; this file is not.
#
# The first three are read at module scope and throw if missing or empty, so
# the app does not render at all without them -- in a browser that surfaces as
# a blank page, and under Playwright as "promise was garbage collected", which
# names neither the file nor the variable. Hence this file.

# Supabase, auth only. Both values are public by design: they are compiled into
# the JS bundle and shipped to every browser. They live in .env.local to keep
# them out of the repo, not because they are secret.
# Project Settings -> API in the Supabase dashboard.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# The Hono API server. http://localhost:3000 for local development, and that
# same value is fine for a guest walkthrough, which makes no API calls -- any
# call that did happen would fail loudly rather than pass silently.
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Optional. Conversation with Hana is shelved (DR-023) and stays off unless
# this is set; do not enable it without asking.
# VITE_HANA_ENABLED=

# Optional, for the server and for a signed-in walkthrough.
# FRONTEND_URL=http://localhost:4173

# Optional. Set both and `pnpm walkthrough` signs in first, which lifts it from
# guest (Book One) to free (Book Four). Leave unset to walk as a guest.
# WALKTHROUGH_EMAIL=
# WALKTHROUGH_PASSWORD=
